{
	"name": "Skirmisher",
	"type": "archetype",
	"img": "icons/skills/melee/strike-sword-dagger-runes-red.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>While most rogues and rakes understand a decent amount of what it means to be in a fight, few learn what it means to be an actual warrior on the field of battle. Those who do tend to favor slipping away from whatever group of people press-ganged them into warfare to return to a life of ease. Not so with the Skirmisher.</p><p>Skirmishers on a battlefield tend to act as lightly armed soldiers who weave in and out of danger alongside their allies. As archers, they can be deadly. But a knife on the battlefield finds the chinks in armor all the more easily.</p><p><strong>Table: Skirmisher</strong></p><table border=\"1\"><colgroup><col><col></colgroup><thead><tr style=\"text-align: center;\"><td>Level</td><td>Features</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr style=\"text-align: center;\"><td>3rd</td><td><p>@UUID[Compendium.a5e-martial-artistry.class-features.Item.oEZqhRG8pCpfyZab]{Bonus Proficiencies} @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-class-features.Item.AxXyQ9THUnKhBbAz]{Skirmish}</p></td></tr><tr style=\"text-align: center;\"><td>9th</td><td><p>@UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-class-features.Item.t2LHKCxQQu0TZYfW]{Doublestrike}</p></td></tr><tr style=\"text-align: center;\"><td>13th</td><td><p>@UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-class-features.Item.EJg7DSZLAskLLLzC]{Assess the Field}</p></td></tr><tr style=\"text-align: center;\"><td>17th</td><td>@UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-class-features.Item.lmQcg2PiOCi1ujJT]{Fade into Violence}</td></tr></tbody></table>",
